==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|mane|g=f}}, from {{inh|de|goh|mana|g=f}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*manō||mane}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*mon-||neck}}. In Middle High German there existed a secondary variant {{m|gmh|man|g=m}}, whence the plural {{m|gmh|mene}}. The modern form {{m|de||Mähne}} is from this plural (or from its merger with the original form {{m|gmh||mane}}).

